course: dictionary
lesson: 10261
title: Too: four meanings in one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word too is small, but its meaning changes with the words around it. Read the context to decide which meaning you need. «I want to come too.» Here too means also, as well.
explain: «The bag is too heavy to lift.» Here too means so much that something cannot happen. Ask yourself: what can't happen? You cannot lift the bag. Try swapping in "so heavy that" and see if it still makes sense.
explain: «Not too bad» means not very bad. But «Too bad, they're mine» is rough and sarcastic: it means I don't care that you are upset. The tone and the situation show which meaning the speaker means.
fact: Too can mean also or as well: «I want to come too.»
fact: Too can mean more than is wanted or good: «too hot», «too many».
fact: «Too ... to» means so much that something cannot happen: «too deep to swim».
fact: «Me too» means I agree, and «too right» means I agree completely (casual, in Australia, New Zealand and the UK).
fact: In formal writing, authors may use likewise, additionally or excessively instead of too.
exercise: «Older children in big families often help a lot, but if it gets too much, tell a parent or a teacher.» What does too much mean here? | Not very much | *More than someone can cope with | Very funny | Also, as well
exercise: «Some hot springs smell of it too.» What does too mean here? | So much that it cannot happen | More than is good | *Also, as well | Not very
exercise: Which phrase means so much that something cannot happen? | Not too bad | Too bad | *Too deep to swim | Me too
test: Lily says, «Not too bad.» What does she mean? | It is extremely bad | I feel very ill | Bad news, too | *It is not very bad
test: Sam's friend says he loves football. Sam says, «Me too.» What does Sam mean? | I want to play tomorrow only | *I agree, I love football too | Football is too expensive | I hate football
exam: «The bag is too heavy for me to carry.» Which meaning of too is used here? | *So much that something cannot happen | Not very | Yes, I agree completely | Also, as well
